@startuml spark-apps-security
title Spark applications (dq-app / dataset-app) - authorization

skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #444444
    ActorBorderColor #2C5D8A
    LifeCycleBorderColor #2C5D8A
    ParticipantBorderColor #2C5D8A
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #E8F0F8
}

participant "task-executor-svc" as TE
participant "task-proxy-for-spark" as PX
participant "Spark cluster\n(Standalone/K8s/YARN)" as SC
participant "Spark driver\n(dq-app / dataset-app)\nSpring Boot app" as DR
participant "Keycloak\n(realm: lakehouse,\nclient: lakehouse-internal-client)" as KC
participant "Backend services\n(scheduler-svc / config-svc)" as BE

== Job submission ==

TE -> TE : Consume task from Kafka
TE -> KC : client_credentials\n(lakehouse-internal-client)
KC --> TE : access_token
TE -> PX : POST /v1/submissions\nAuthorization: Bearer <token>
note over PX : OAuth2 resource server:\nvalidates JWT like any backend service
PX -> SC : spark-submit (queue adapter)

== Driver execution inside the cluster ==

SC -> DR : Start driver JVM\n(Spring Boot, @ComponentScan includes\norg.lakehouse.security)
note over DR #FFF3D6
    No user security context inside the driver ->
    all callbacks use their own
    client_credentials tokens
end note

DR -> KC : POST /token\ngrant_type=client_credentials
KC --> DR : access_token
DR -> BE : getScheduledTaskDTO / getEffectiveTaskDTO\nget source & task configurations\nAuthorization: Bearer <driver JWT>
BE -> BE : JWT validation + AuditLoggingFilter\n(username = "system")
BE --> DR : Task payload / configurations

DR -> BE : Report results / statuses\n(Bearer token, same flow)

note over SC
    Secret redaction (SparkSessionConfiguration):
    spark.redaction.regex =
    (?i)secret|password|token|access[.]key|credentials|private
end note

legend right
    No tokens/secrets are passed as job arguments
    Driver authenticates itself directly against Keycloak
    Direct submission to a vanilla Spark master
    bypasses OAuth validation (operator's responsibility)
end legend
@enduml
